;; Arbace's addition to package reflect (doc/go/GOI-SPEC.md, "As built: GR9a-c"; the GR9 survey,
;; doc/go/GR9-SURVEY.md, §3.1, its Appendix B the prototype): goi's interpreted named types made
;; at run time as runtime types of their own, with their method sets, so that compiled code, fmt,
;; reflect and the runtime see them as gc's. The runtime resolves the offsets of a descriptor
;; that is in no module through reflectOffs (runtime/type.go); this file makes such descriptors
;; from reflect's own types and helpers, so that a change of internal/abi's layouts is a compile
;; error. It enters every build as an overlay file (bin/jrt overlay), as overlay/go/runtime's do.

